us="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMAZAKI, FUJIO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIDA YOSHITSUGU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMAZAKI FUJIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIDA, YOSHITSUGU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMAZAKI, FUJIO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of treating seeds of grasses, comprising exposing seed rice and seeds of corn to a magnetic field before they are cultivated, and then placing the resultant seeds on a flat plate of gray cast iron to expose them to an electric field; or exposing seed rice and seeds of corn to a magnetic field after they have been exposed to an electric field; or preferably immersing seed rice and seeds of corn in specific water electric-field-treated or magnetic-field-treated in advance, these treatments promoting the germination of the seeds and activating vegetation genes, resulting in an increase in the yield.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention se rapporte à un procédé de traitement de semences de graminées, qui consiste à exposer des plants de riz et des semences de maïs à un champ magnétique avant de les utiliser pour la culture, puis à placer les semences ainsi traitées sur une plaque plate en fonte grise de manière à les exposer à un champ électrique; ou à exposer des plants de riz et des semences de maïs après les avoir exposés à un champ électrique; ou de préférence à immerger ces plants de riz et ces semences de maïs dans une eau particulière soumise préalablement à un champ électrique ou à un champ magnétique. Les traitements en question favorisent la germination des semences et activent les gènes de croissance, ce qui se traduit par un accroissement du rendement.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>